{
  "name": "meta-models",
  "description": "The four Muse Wonder rows (muse-wonder-1.0, its `-contributor` twin, muse-wonder-full-1.0 and its `-contributor` twin) on Pi's built-in `meta` provider, as a `pi/models` config-overlay. They make the whole line the Muse subscription includes selectable in Pi's /model menu; the rows inherit Pi's own meta client, address and /login credential.",
  "contributes": [
    // MUSE WONDER IN PI: ALL FOUR ROWS. Pi ships the `meta` provider with five Muse models and
    // NO Muse Wonder at all, so the model the subscription pays for is unreachable from
    // `/model` without this contribution. A `models.json` row merged onto the built-in
    // provider is exactly what pi supports for this (core/provider-composer.js
    // applyModelsJson, docs/models.md), and it reuses pi's own `meta` client, its
    // `https://api.meta.ai/v1` address and the Muse-subscription login: no `apiKey`, no
    // `api_key_env_name`, no extension installed.
    //
    // `api` IS spelled out and the ADDRESS is not: "openai-responses" is the protocol every
    // Muse model on `meta` speaks, while the base URL and the OAuth credential are the
    // provider's own and are inherited from pi's catalog (the composer takes the matching
    // catalog row's baseUrl when the model states none, and that is https://api.meta.ai/v1).
    //
    // WHY THIS KIND. yolo's pi derive writes no such row for a provider pi ships built in
    // (packs/pi/derive.lua's piOwn), so a `providers.meta.models` declaration has no effect
    // on `pi/models`, and a `models` pack contribution cannot reach it either: an `add` with
    // no `only` is meant to ride a row a built-in provider never gets, while an `only`
    // REPLACES pi's meta menu with the declared rows and enforces it — a different change,
    // and one that hides any model pi adds later. The pi pack owns `pi/models`, so an overlay
    // on that surface is the smallest supported route and the one with no rot. It is an
    // OVERLAY rather than a `config-list` because `thinkingLevelMap.off` has to be JSON
    // `null` — that is how pi is told a model refuses its "off" level — and a config-list
    // `add` entry may hold no null.
    //
    // THE CLEAN FIX IS A PI CATALOG ADDITION, NOT THIS OVERLAY. These rows are a workaround
    // for Pi's static baked catalog plus the pi.dev shard, both of which carry the five Muse
    // Sparks and no Wonder. The right home for them is Pi's own model catalog (the same place
    // the Spark rows come from); this pack exists because that table cannot be edited from
    // here. Delete it once the rows are in the catalog.
    //
    // THE FOUR IDS ARE THE WHOLE WONDER LINE, from a live probe of this account's Model API
    // credential (2026-10-12): `GET /v1/models` lists muse-wonder-1.0,
    // muse-wonder-1.0-contributor, muse-wonder-full-1.0 and muse-wonder-full-1.0-contributor;
    // `GET /v1/models/<id>` answers 200 for each; and a `/v1/responses` call completes on each
    // of the four. `muse-wonder-full` (bare), `muse-wonder-1.0-full` and `muse-wonder-pro` are
    // 404 `model_not_found`, so no other spelling is wanted. META'S OWN AVAILABILITY TABLE IS
    // KNOWN-WRONG FOR FULL: it says Muse Wonder Full is available only in Muse Code, yet its
    // Model API id resolves and answers here on a Power Usage plan.
    //
    // NAMES ARE SPELLED OUT, never derived from catalogue metadata, because the catalogue's
    // own `name` for `muse-wonder-full-1.0-contributor` is WRONG — it reads
    // "muse-wonder-1.0-contributor", colliding with the id it is not.
    //
    // ENTITLEMENT-DRIVEN. Wonder itself is on every plan; `muse-wonder-full-1.0` is the
    // higher-capability variant, on Power Usage and Maximum Usage only, so a plan without one
    // of those will not have Full and a call for it is that account's refusal to report, not
    // this pack's. The two `-contributor` ids are Contributor mode (content may train future
    // Meta models) rather than a different capability.
    //
    // WINDOWS ARE THE CLI CATALOGUE'S OWN (`GET https://api.meta.ai/muse-code/models`, read
    // 2026-10-12), which reports context 1007997 and max output 128000 for all four ids.
    // Meta's docs page states a 1,048,576-token context window and pi's Muse Spark rows carry
    // 1048576/131072; the CLI catalogue figure is used here because it is the limit the
    // endpoint enforces, and the docs figure is recorded rather than silently dropped.
    // Stating `maxTokens` at all matters: pi's default for a row that says nothing is 16384.
    //
    // COST. `muse-wonder-1.0` carries Meta's published Standard-mode rates -- $4.00/M input,
    // $20.00/M output, $0.20/M cached input, no cache-write charge. THE OTHER THREE CARRY
    // ZEROS, AND ZERO IS NOT "FREE": Meta publishes no per-token rate for
    // `muse-wonder-full-1.0` (subscription-metered -- its pricing page has no Full row at
    // all) and none for either `-contributor` id. For those three, pi's cost figure is
    // meaningless: it reports $0 for models the subscription funds.
    //
    // `reasoning: true` and the thinking map follow Meta's reasoning doc: `"none"` is refused
    // for Muse Wonder (HTTP 400), so `off` is null, and the CLI catalogue lists a `max`
    // variant for all four ids, so `max` maps to `"max"`. `input` carries image because Meta
    // states Wonder and Spark "take the same requests".
    {
      "kind": "config-overlay",
      "surface": "pi/models",
      "config": {
        "managed": {
          "providers": {
            "meta": {
              "models": [
                {
                  "id": "muse-wonder-1.0",
                  "name": "Muse Wonder 1.0",
                  "api": "openai-responses",
                  "reasoning": true,
                  "thinkingLevelMap": {
                    "off": null,
                    "minimal": "minimal",
                    "low": "low",
                    "medium": "medium",
                    "high": "high",
                    "xhigh": "xhigh",
                    "max": "max"
                  },
                  "input": ["text", "image"],
                  "contextWindow": 1007997,
                  "maxTokens": 128000,
                  "cost": {
                    "input": 4.0,
                    "output": 20.0,
                    "cacheRead": 0.2,
                    "cacheWrite": 0
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "muse-wonder-1.0-contributor",
                  "name": "Muse Wonder 1.0 Contributor",
                  "api": "openai-responses",
                  "reasoning": true,
                  "thinkingLevelMap": {
                    "off": null,
                    "minimal": "minimal",
                    "low": "low",
                    "medium": "medium",
                    "high": "high",
                    "xhigh": "xhigh",
                    "max": "max"
                  },
                  "input": ["text", "image"],
                  "contextWindow": 1007997,
                  "maxTokens": 128000,
                  "cost": {
                    "input": 0,
                    "output": 0,
                    "cacheRead": 0,
                    "cacheWrite": 0
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "muse-wonder-full-1.0",
                  "name": "Muse Wonder Full 1.0",
                  "api": "openai-responses",
                  "reasoning": true,
                  "thinkingLevelMap": {
                    "off": null,
                    "minimal": "minimal",
                    "low": "low",
                    "medium": "medium",
                    "high": "high",
                    "xhigh": "xhigh",
                    "max": "max"
                  },
                  "input": ["text", "image"],
                  "contextWindow": 1007997,
                  "maxTokens": 128000,
                  "cost": {
                    "input": 0,
                    "output": 0,
                    "cacheRead": 0,
                    "cacheWrite": 0
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "muse-wonder-full-1.0-contributor",
                  "name": "Muse Wonder Full 1.0 Contributor",
                  "api": "openai-responses",
                  "reasoning": true,
                  "thinkingLevelMap": {
                    "off": null,
                    "minimal": "minimal",
                    "low": "low",
                    "medium": "medium",
                    "high": "high",
                    "xhigh": "xhigh",
                    "max": "max"
                  },
                  "input": ["text", "image"],
                  "contextWindow": 1007997,
                  "maxTokens": 128000,
                  "cost": {
                    "input": 0,
                    "output": 0,
                    "cacheRead": 0,
                    "cacheWrite": 0
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
